    "summary": "High‑energy Greek Theatre '82 with monster Scarlet>Fire and epic jams",
    "review": "May 23, 1982 at Berkeley’s Greek Theatre is one of the spring ’82 high points – a night that crackles from the opening Shakedown Street all the way through a blistering 33‑minute Scarlet Begonias > Fire on the Mountain and marathon Estimated Prophet > Eyes of the World > The Other One stretches.  The band is locked in, with Brent Mydland’s organ and his mic’d Harley adding extra grit to “Little Red Rooster,” while Bob Weir’s guitar sits front‑and‑center, driving funk‑filled jams on Shakedown and the second‑set flights.  Jerry’s vocals are relaxed (though a bit thin early on) and his lead work stays solid throughout, Phil’s bass anchors the improvisations, and the dual drummers lock in tight, even tossing in a novelty biker interaction during the drum break.  Multiple soundboard sources capture this energy with crystal‑clear separation, making the Miller SBD the definitive listening choice.",
